        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The <strong class="text-white">best concrete floor coating</strong> depends on the floor. For a typical garage, <strong class="text-white">Rust-Oleum EpoxyShield Professional</strong> is the right balance of durability and DIY forgiveness. For a floor you want to forget about for a decade, a <strong class="text-white">polyaspartic system</strong> is worth the cost and the short pot life. For a basement or patio, a textured one-part coating gives you the slip resistance that matters there.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Whatever you choose, the outcome is decided by preparation. <strong class="text-white">Rent a grinder instead of acid etching</strong>, <strong class="text-white">test for moisture with a taped plastic square</strong>, and <strong class="text-white">stay off it with a vehicle for the full cure</strong>. Those three steps prevent nearly every coating failure there is.
